1903–04 was the 16th season of competitive football for [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic FC]]. They competed in the [[Scottish First Division]],<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.londonhearts.com/scores/a1900/celtic1904.htm|title=Results for Celtic for 1903-04|website=www.londonhearts.com}}</ref> in which they placed third.

Celtic won the [[Scottish Cup]] with a 3–2 win over [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]] in which [[Jimmy Quinn (footballer, born 1878)|Jimmy Quinn]] scored a hat-trick. It was Celtic's fourth Scottish Cup victory and, together with their four league titles so far, their 8th major trophy.

[[Willie Orr]], who had been playing for the Glasgow team since 1897, became Celtic's fourth ever captain, as he succeeded [[Sandy McMahon]] who had left Celtic the previous season.

